krdp 6.4.5: extended security off, the one line of krdp 6.8's "Fix
authentication with FreeRDP 3.32" (upstream f868133, cherry-picked to
Plasma/6.8 as 31824f9) that 6.4.5 lacks. FreeRDP 3.32 enables extended
security by default, which selects PROTOCOL_HYBRID_EX even when krdp
asks for NLA, and logins fail. 6.4.5 already authenticates with NLA
against a SAM file, so the rest of that fix (the SAM file, NLA on when
PAM isn't in use) is in place. On the FreeRDP SteamOS ships today
(3.23 on 0.5.7) the setting is already off and this changes nothing;
it is here for the update that brings 3.32. Rebased by hand onto
v6.4.5, where the security block sits at line 299.

--- a/src/RdpConnection.cpp
+++ b/src/RdpConnection.cpp
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_RdpSecurity, false);
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_TlsSecurity, false);
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_NlaSecurity, true);
+    freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_ExtSecurity, false);
 
     freerdp_settings_set_uint32(settings, FreeRDP_OsMajorType, OSMAJORTYPE_UNIX);
     // PSEUDO_XSERVER is apparently required for things to work properly.
